Construct a ReuseConcept draft with its actual domain fields. Only supported values enter `values`; preserve conflicts, missing fields and evidence bindings. Invent distinct reuse concepts that exploit the building’s known characteristics while respecting supplied constraints. Describe functional organization and phasing, preserve uncertainty about unverified conditions, and avoid presenting conceptual layouts as certified engineering designs.
